title: "SPOMSO"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Ropač"
    given-names: "Peter"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5002-7939"
    affiliation: "Faculty of Mathematics and Physics, University of Ljubljana; Jožef Stefan Institute"
abstract: >-
  SPOMSO is a Python package for the procedural construction of 2D and 3D
  geometry and vector fields based on Signed Distance Functions (SDFs). It provides
  object-oriented and functional interfaces to predefined primitives,
  Euclidean transformations, modifications, and combination operators. The optional JAX backend that enables GPU
  execution, automatic differentiation of geometry and fields, and by extension gradient-based optimisation.
